        "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/5/19/iran-war-live-trump-says-iran-attack-postponed-at-request-of-gulf-allies?traffic_source=rss",
        "orario": "02:00",
        "timestamp": 1779148800,
        "contenuto_esteso": "8 Updates Auto-updates live-orange 9m ago ( 01:15 GMT ) US Senate Democrats to force eighth vote on War Powers Resolution US Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer announced that the legislative body will force an eighth vote on a War Powers Resolution this week, aiming to curb Trump’s ability to wage war on Iran. Posting on X, Schumer wrote: “This week, for the EIGHTH time, Senate Democrats are forcing a vote on our War Powers Resolution to withdraw our troops from hostilities with Iran.” He called on Senate Republicans to pass the resolution, end the war, and “get our troops out of harm’s way”. The US Constitution dictates that Congress, not the president, can declare war. This week, for the EIGHTH time, @SenateDems are forcing a vote on our War Powers Resolution to withdraw our troops from hostilities with Iran. @SenateGOP : Support our War Powers Resolution. End the war. Get our troops out of harm’s way. — Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) May 18, 2026 live-orange 24m ago ( 01:00 GMT ) Trump maintains sense of ‘limbo’, while ‘threatening imminent action’ By Mike Hanna Trump says he was approached by Gulf leaders to postpone an attack on Iran, an attack which, publicly, nobody really knew about. He said, subsequent to that TruthSocial posting, that he would delay the attack for possibly two or three days, but implying that there had been progress in mediation efforts with Iran that could bear fruit in the coming days. But he also added that he would order the secretary of defence to be ready for immediate combat, should he so desire. So, President Trump is maintaining the sense of limbo; at the same time, threatening imminent action, [while] at the other hand, trying to get some form of negotiation or agreement going. And he’s facing the potential fallout, both domestically and internationally, should he have to resume this war. live-orange 39m ago ( 00:45 GMT ) Hezbollah claims multiple attacks on Israeli forces in southern Lebanon Hezbollah says its fighters launched 14 attacks on Israeli forces inside southern Lebanon on Monday. In a statement, the group detailed offensive operations using explosive drones, rockets and artillery shells, with attacks primarily targeted at gatherings of Israeli soldiers and military vehicles in several Lebanese border towns and valleys. Advertisement live-orange 54m ago ( 00:30 GMT ) Here’s the latest from Trump Here are some of the latest updates from Trump regarding the war on Iran: Trump told reporters at the White House on Monday afternoon that there is “a very good ⁠chance” that Saudi Arabia, Qatar and the UAE could reach a deal to end the war soon. “If we can do that without bombing the hell out of them, I ‌would be very happy,” Trump said. The US president again emphasised his primary condition that Iran does not obtain a nuclear weapon, but said the US would “be probably satisfied also” if its allies in the region were satisfied. Trump further specified that he had agreed to wait two or three days before bombing Iran after announcing he had delayed an attack planned for Tuesday. live-orange 1h ago ( 00:15 GMT ) Israeli air strike hits building in Tyre after displacement threat The Palestinian Information Center reports that a violent air attack launched by Israeli aircraft hit a building in the al-Mushaqqa area of the Tyre district in southern Lebanon. The bombardment occurred after the Israeli military issued a forced displacement order for al-Mushaqqa in the past hour. غارة عنيفة شنتها طائرات الاحتلال على مبنى في منطقة #المعشوق قضاء صور جنوبي #لبنان — المركز الفلسطيني للإعلام (@PalinfoAr) May 18, 2026 Translation: A violent raid launched by occupation aircraft on a building in the al-Mushaqqa area, Tyre district, southern #Lebanon. live-orange 1h ago ( 00:07 GMT ) WATCH: Palestinians in Gaza welcome flotilla aid attempts Palestinians in Gaza have welcomed attempts by the latest flotilla to break Israel’s devastating blockade. They also expressed hope that participants in the aid mission would remain safe, as Israeli forces seized their ships. Al Jazeera’s Tareq Abu Azzoum reports from Gaza. live-orange 1h ago ( 00:03 GMT ) A recap of recent developments Trump said he has delayed attacking Iran by two to three days because Saudi Arabia, Qatar and the UAE said they were close to reaching a deal with Tehran. Israeli attacks on Lebanon have killed more than 3,000 people since March 2, the Lebanese Health Ministry said. Israeli forces have detained hundreds of people participating in a Gaza-bound aid flotilla, including Margaret Connolly, the sister of Ireland’s president. The US military says it “redirected” at least 85 ships during its blockade on Iranian ports, while Iran’s Persian Gulf Strait Authority said any ships transiting the Strait of Hormuz without its permission “will be considered illegal”. Qatari Prime Minister Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman bin Jassim Al Thani has expressed “full support” for Pakistan-led mediation efforts to end “the crisis through peaceful means”. live-orange 1h ago ( 00:00 GMT ) Welcome Hello, and welcome to our live coverage of the ceasefire in the US-Israel war on Iran and Israel’s attacks on Lebanon. Stay with us for the latest news and analysis from across the Middle East and beyond. You can find our updates from Monday, May 18, here ."
